    {
      "title": "API Keys, Sessions and Tokens",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "API Keys, Sessions and Tokens",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Authn vs Authz",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Authentication",
                "Authorization"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Asks",
                  "Who are you?",
                  "What may you do?"
                ],
                [
                  "Fails",
                  "{red:401}",
                  "{red:403}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Three Credentials",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==API key==: static secret naming an app",
                "Header `X-API-Key: <key>` or `Authorization: Bearer <key>`, never the URL",
                "==Session==: server stores state, cookie holds opaque ID; revoke = delete record",
                "==Token==: signed, self-contained, no server record; scales, hard to revoke before expiry"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "API key",
                "Session",
                "Token"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Is",
                  "machine identity, no user",
                  "stateful, cookie-bound",
                  "stateless, carries claims"
                ],
                [
                  "Life",
                  "long-lived",
                  "server decides",
                  "short-lived"
                ],
                [
                  "Revoke",
                  "rotate",
                  "easy",
                  "hard"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Never",
              "text": "A key in the URL leaks into logs."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**401 vs 403?** 401 not authenticated; 403 authenticated but not allowed",
                "**Sessions easier to revoke?** Delete the server record; a JWT lives until `exp`",
                "**API key over OAuth?** Server-to-server calls with no user context"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "JWT Structure and Pitfalls",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "JWT Structure and Pitfalls",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Structure and Claims",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==header.payload.signature==, three base64url parts",
                "Header holds `alg`, `typ`; payload holds claims"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Claim",
                "Means"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`iss`",
                  "issuer"
                ],
                [
                  "`sub`",
                  "subject"
                ],
                [
                  "`aud`",
                  "audience"
                ],
                [
                  "`exp`",
                  "expiry, Unix seconds"
                ],
                [
                  "`iat`",
                  "issued at"
                ],
                [
                  "`nbf`",
                  "not before"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Verify Every Request",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Check ==signature==, `exp`, `iss`, `aud`",
                "Signed is **not encrypted**: payload is readable, so no secrets or PII"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "HS256",
                "RS256"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Key",
                  "one shared secret",
                  "private signs, public verifies"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Pitfalls",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Accepting `alg: none`",
                "Trusting the header `alg` instead of pinning it",
                "Algorithm confusion: RS256 key used as HS256 secret",
                "Long expiry with no revocation",
                "JWT in localStorage, where XSS reads it"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Readable but tamper-proof?** Base64 is encoding; any edit breaks the signature.",
                "**alg=none attack?** Forged unsigned token; stop it by pinning the allowed alg.",
                "**HS256 vs RS256?** HS256 within one service; RS256 when others must verify.",
                "**Revoke a JWT?** Short expiry plus a denylist, or rotate keys."
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "purple"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "OAuth 2.0 Flows and Scopes",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "OAuth 2.0 Flows and Scopes",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What OAuth 2.0 Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Delegated authorization==: limited access, no password shared",
                "Roles: resource owner, client, authorization server, resource server"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Flows",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "/authorize",
                    "sub": "user consents",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Callback",
                    "sub": "returns code",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "POST /token",
                    "sub": "code + code_verifier",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Access token",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Flow",
                "Use",
                "Status"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Auth Code + PKCE",
                  "web, SPA, mobile",
                  "{green:use}"
                ],
                [
                  "Client Credentials",
                  "machine; id + secret to /token",
                  "{green:use}"
                ],
                [
                  "Implicit, Password",
                  "none",
                  "{red:deprecated}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Send `code_challenge` = ==BASE64URL(SHA256(code_verifier))== up front",
                "Add `code_challenge_method=S256`; verifier goes in the exchange",
                "Stolen code is useless; use for all ==public clients=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Scopes and state",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Scopes limit a token, e.g. `read:orders`, `write:orders`",
                "Requested in `scope`, approved by the user",
                "Resource server ==enforces== scopes on each call",
                "`state` parameter blocks CSRF on the redirect"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why PKCE?** Stolen code is useless without the verifier",
                "**Backend job, no user?** Client Credentials",
                "**Scope?** Limits the token; resource server enforces it",
                "**Why drop Implicit?** Token exposed in the redirect URL"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Refresh Tokens and Token Lifecycle",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Refresh Tokens and Token Lifecycle",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Two Tokens",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Access",
                "Refresh"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Life",
                  "==5-15 min==",
                  "long-lived"
                ],
                [
                  "Sent to",
                  "every API call",
                  "`/token` only"
                ],
                [
                  "Request",
                  "bearer header",
                  "`grant_type=refresh_token`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Rotation and Storage",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Refresh used",
                    "sub": "POST /token",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "New pair",
                    "sub": "new refresh token",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Old one dead",
                    "sub": "invalidated",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Old one reused",
                    "sub": "theft: revoke family",
                    "ink": "red"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Store server-side or in an ==HttpOnly, Secure, SameSite== cookie",
                "Never in `localStorage` or logs"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Revocation and Token Type",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Opaque",
                "JWT"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Check",
                  "introspection call",
                  "verified locally"
                ],
                [
                  "Revoke",
                  "{green:at once}",
                  "{red:valid until exp}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Revoking",
              "text": "Delete the refresh token on the server. Access tokens live until `exp` unless you keep a ==denylist== or use introspection, so keep them short."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Why split?** A leaked access token dies fast; the refresh token never rides on API calls",
                "**Rotation?** Each use issues a new refresh token; reuse of an old one revokes the family",
                "**Storage?** Refresh: server or HttpOnly cookie; access: memory, never `localStorage`"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "HTTPS and Transport Security",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "HTTPS and Transport Security",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. HTTPS and the handshake",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "HTTPS = HTTP over ==TLS==: encryption, integrity, server authentication",
                "Without it, keys, cookies and tokens can be **sniffed**",
                "Cert checks: trusted ==CA== signed it, domain matches, unexpired, not revoked",
                "Never disable verification, e.g. `verify=False`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client hello",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Certificate",
                    "sub": "from server",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Validate",
                    "sub": "CA chain + hostname",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Session key",
                    "sub": "symmetric",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Encrypted data",
                    "ink": "black"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Cookie flags and HSTS",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Flag",
                "Stops"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Secure`",
                  "cookie sent over plain HTTP"
                ],
                [
                  "`HttpOnly`",
                  "JS reading it (XSS theft)"
                ],
                [
                  "`SameSite=Lax/Strict`",
                  "cross-site sends (CSRF)"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Set-Cookie: sid=abc; Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax",
                "Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000"
              ],
              "note": "HSTS makes browsers use HTTPS only"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Also redirect HTTP to HTTPS"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. URLs and Interview Point",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "No keys in URLs",
              "text": "Query strings leak into **logs**, browser history and `Referer` headers. Use the `Authorization` header."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**TLS handshake achieves?** Authenticated server, shared session key, encrypted traffic",
                "**Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite stop?** Plain-HTTP sends, JS theft, CSRF",
                "**Key in query string?** It leaks into logs, history, Referer"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Auth Cheat Sheet",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Auth Cheat Sheet",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Pick the Mechanism",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Need",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Server-to-server identity",
                  "==API key=="
                ],
                [
                  "First-party web app",
                  "==Session cookie=="
                ],
                [
                  "APIs, SPAs, third parties",
                  "==JWT== or OAuth access token"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. JWT and OAuth",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Pin alg==, never trust the header",
                "Verify ==signature==, `exp`, `iss`, `aud`",
                "Short-lived, ==no secrets== in payload"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Client",
                "Flow"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "User-facing",
                  "==Auth Code + PKCE=="
                ],
                [
                  "Machine",
                  "==Client Credentials=="
                ],
                [
                  "Never",
                  "{red:Implicit, Password}"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Tokens and Transport",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Access token about ==15 minutes==",
                "Refresh token ==rotated==, stored ==HttpOnly==",
                "Revoke on ==logout== and on ==reuse detection==",
                "Always ==HTTPS + HSTS==",
                "Secrets in ==env vars or a vault==, never git or URLs",
                "Leaked key: ==rotate immediately=="
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Login to API call?** HTTPS, Auth Code + PKCE, short access token, API checks `exp`, `aud`, scope",
                "**Leaked token first?** Revoke it and its refresh family, then rotate keys",
                "**Sessions or JWTs?** Sessions for first-party web: easy revoke"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An attacker edits the JWT payload from role=user to role=admin and keeps the old signature. A correct server does what?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Rejects it with ==401==: the signature no longer matches the payload.",
                "The payload is readable by anyone, but changing it breaks the signature."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "Refresh token rotation is on. An old refresh token is presented a second time. What happens?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Treated as ==theft==: the server revokes the whole token family.",
                "The real user and the attacker both have to log in again."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A valid token with only scope read:orders calls DELETE /orders/7. Which status, and who decides?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "==403==: the caller is authenticated but not authorized.",
                "The resource server must enforce the scope on every call."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
